stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Active: state and issuer checked; PS256 ID Token verified; one-use JTI and sid-bound session committed
    Active --> Expired: absolute_expires_at passes (derived)
    Expired --> Active: prompt=none callback renews the same sid-bound session
    Active --> Revoked: Base App POST sign-out commits local revocation
    Active --> Revoked: verified Visa Back-Channel Logout commits
    Expired --> Revoked: verified Visa Back-Channel Logout commits
    [*] --> Revoked: Back-Channel Logout commits unknown-sid tombstone
    Revoked --> [*]

    note right of Active
        Effective only while the RP session and OP sid binding
        are unrevoked and absolute_expires_at is in the future.
        Expired is derived at read time, not stored. Renewal uses a new
        front-channel ID Token with prompt=none and the same OP sid.
    end note
